WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.170
Sell, serve and stay safe with WhatsApp Business.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.100
This is the video for module four of WhatsApp for Communication and Business.

3
00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:16.330
WhatsApp Business is a free app made for small businesses. Your customers chat with you from their normal WhatsApp.

4
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:24.380
A complete profile tells a new customer who you are, what you sell and when you are open, before you type a word.

5
00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.130
Four tools help you answer faster and never forget an order.

6
00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:35.290
And because money moves through these chats, you will learn the habits that stop most scams.

7
00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:48.400
Step one. Install WhatsApp Business from the Play Store or App Store, developer WhatsApp LLC. It is free. Anyone selling a blue tick or activation is not from WhatsApp.

8
00:00:49.650 --> 00:01:03.620
Step two. Use a separate business SIM if you can, so family chats stay private. If customers already know your number, back up first, then verify that number in the Business app and it offers to move your chats.

9
00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:11.250
Step three. Enter your business name exactly as customers know it, choose a category, and add your logo.

10
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:19.760
Step four. Turn on two-step verification straight away. A business account is a valuable target for fraudsters.

11
00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:33.190
Step five. In Business tools, find your short link and QR code. Nkechi in Aba printed her QR code by her pharmacy counter, and now customers order refills before they come.

12
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:41.220
Open Business tools, Business profile. Start with your logo on a plain background, or a clear shop photo.

13
00:01:42.470 --> 00:01:55.760
For the description use this formula: what you offer, who it is for, where or how, and one action. For example, handmade shea butter creams for dry skin, delivery in Abuja, tap Catalog to order.

14
00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:04.480
Add an address or landmark and your real business hours. Your away message can use these hours, so keep them accurate.

15
00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:14.970
And be truthful. Never claim NAFDAC, SON or CAC registration you do not have. False claims lose trust and can bring legal trouble.

16
00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:26.330
The catalogue is your shop window. Use clear daylight photos on a plain background. Prices change often, so update them, or write Price on request.

17
00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:42.580
A greeting message goes automatically to new customers. Keep it to three or four short lines with one action. Set the away message to Outside of business hours, never Always send, or customers think you are never available.

18
00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:55.470
Quick replies save typing the same thing fifty times. Type a slash and a shortcut, like slash pay, and the full message appears. Make them for your five most common questions.

19
00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:09.160
Kemi runs Kemi's Kitchen in Lagos. One Friday, 23 office workers message her between 8am and 10am. Each first-time customer gets her greeting automatically.

20
00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.330
She labels each chat New order.

21
00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:23.780
After sending slash pay, she moves it to Pending payment. At 10:30 she filters by that label, sees 4 chats, and sends each a polite reminder.

22
00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:30.960
She labels a chat Paid only after confirming the money in her bank app, not from a screenshot alone.

23
00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:37.820
After delivery, Order complete. All 23 orders are tracked, and nothing is forgotten.

24
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:51.930
Rose sells phone accessories in Computer Village, Ikeja. A buyer orders goods worth 38,000 naira, arrives, shows a transfer screenshot and says, please hurry, my driver is waiting.

25
00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.210
Rose notices the pressure. That is a red flag.

26
00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:04.780
She opens her own Moniepoint app to check incoming transfers. No payment of 38,000 naira has arrived.

27
00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:16.950
She politely says goods are released only when the money shows. The buyer leaves. Rose reports and blocks the number, and adds that rule to her slash pay quick reply.

28
00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:23.830
Three rules stop most scams. Never share your six-digit code or two-step PIN.

29
00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:28.920
Never release goods or refunds until money reflects in your own banking app.

30
00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:35.880
And if a new number with a relative's photo asks for urgent money, call that person on a number you already know.

31
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:52.730
To remember. Use a business SIM and turn on two-step verification. Fill a complete, truthful profile. Switch on your catalogue, greeting, quick replies and labels. And always check payments in your own app, never by screenshot.

32
00:04:53.980 --> 00:05:03.900
Now set up your shop. Fill every profile field, add five products to your catalogue, create four quick replies, and update your payment reply with the rule.

33
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.400
Then continue with the lessons below.
